            0.466,
            0.454
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We have seen in the previous sections that all metals are not equally reactive. We checked the reactivity of various metals with oxygen, water and acids. But all metals do not react with these reagents. So we were not able to put all the metal samples we had collected in decreasing order of their reactivity. Displacement reactions studied in Chapter 1 give better evidence about the reactivity of metals. It is simple and easy if metal A displaces",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
